WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.120
Previously on Godzilla.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:14.610
It was human size!

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:21.460
It was for me.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:44.200
This Godzilla drone was quickly destroyed by the U.S. military.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:49.060
However, there are new reports of yet another creature wreaking havoc off the shores of Japan.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.020
That should have been me on the 6 o'clock news.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.040
Yeah, well, it's kind of hard to get your stuff on the air

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.400
when a bunch of stormtroopers grab your camera and trample your First Amendment rights.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:01:59.980
You are...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.520
No right calling Major Hicks.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.180
That creature wasn't a threat to anybody.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.370
You think I'd actually...

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.370
Hey, hey, hey, we didn't even see Godzilla, okay?

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.230
Until, like, two seconds before the cavalry showed up.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.930
If you didn't call Hicks, who did?

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.100
Maybe your little girlfriend didn't think you could keep Godzilla under control.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.010
What's the matter, news Twinkie?

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:20.730
Can't handle a little competition?

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.650
All right, goodbye!

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:24.370
Shut up.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.620
You and I talk, now.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:33.960
I know what you're thinking.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.740
How could I just destroy the scientific find of the century?

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.070
The insight we could have obtained from that creature is immeasurable.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.660
You think I didn't consider that?

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.660
But I also had to think about how many lives that insight might cost.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.900
Go back to scooping up worms.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.540
It'll be a lot safer for everyone.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.660
You're not arresting me?

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:53.620
You're disappointed?

00:02:58.660 --> 00:02:59.980
Luck outing our Benedict Arnold.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.960
I tapped into Hicks' phone records.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.480
The call was untraceable.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:04.200
Ta-da!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.000
Craven and I are ready for Jamaica.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.140
I got my flu shots.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.160
If there is another creature down there, we'll be on top of it.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.380
Fine. Randy and I will join you as soon as possible.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:31.750
Private party?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:34.290
Enough.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:48.230
Who are you?

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.020
Monique Dupré.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.060
I believe you know my associates in the insurance game.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.140
Have you and your French Secret Service pals been shadowing me the whole time?

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.200
You're a spy?

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.880
We did what we felt was necessary.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.140
You? You're the one who called in the airstrike.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.700
Had you done your job properly, that creature would never have been born.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.380
What gives you the right to...

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.560
And now the moral debate begins.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:18.630
Might we postpone until we have dispensed with the latest mutation?

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.870
Oh, no. I'm done cleaning up after your government.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.180
Ha! Your angst is almost European.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.630
But please, join me in looking at...

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.100
How do you say, the big picture?

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:40.780
I can provide you with a state-of-the-art research vessel, as well as weaponry and protection.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.640
Don't know about you, Efe, but I feel safer already.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.360
We leave first thing in the morning. I'm in charge.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.970
Visualizing analytic protocols. Analyze.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:12.160
sample now remind me to kill that teenage punk for messing with Nigel's

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:25.300
linguistic software that thing sensation something's in here

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:40.880
it looks like this tar was draining it but why this is state of the art beggars cannot be choosers

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:47.600
monsieur tetapolis that's dr tetapolis and i don't recall begging you for anything

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:59.650
a few one sheets some chips a cooler and we're good to go ahoy matey

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:08.180
permission aboard nice rack what's it called off limits how come everybody keeps doing that

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:12.820
you want to tell me why craven and that red-headed cupid all booked a flight to jamaica how did you

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:18.490
know i have my sources they find anything yet classified how many girlfriends you need to do

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:27.270
your talking for you nikki the data suggests that while draining the fish's electrolytes

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.890
the tar was also keeping it alive

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.890
Why would it do that?

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:41.510
Any chance of hitting Montego Bay before the turn of the next century?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.660
I'm sorry, Captain. The warp drive cannot take anymore.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.400
Nice thrust.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:55.550
What's the word?

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.970
Well, we analyzed the tar. Amino acids reading right off the chart.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:04.470
And the fish we found trapped inside, completely drained of electrolytes.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:08.540
Sounds like the tar is part of some kind of predigested process.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.080
Yeah, we're thinking external stomach.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.300
Once the food is digested, the tar is probably reabsorbed into the predator's body.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.860
What kind of creature are we dealing with?

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:14.560
We are doing everything in our power. Please, remain calm.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:21.300
There must be something you can do, Mr. Ambassador. We're talking about American citizens.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:26.600
We're doing everything we can, Dr. Teutopolis, but this is still a local problem.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.230
I told you it would be a waste of time.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.380
Get this through your head.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.100
Those are my people out there,

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.450
and I'm not resting until I find them.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.220
We have a winner.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.160
I locked onto Nigel's distress signal.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.000
Once I pinpoint the little bot,

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:47.360
I should be able to retrieve him.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.120
They're alive!

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:06.880
Subjects remain unconscious,

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:11.230
attempting to break down the tar's enzymes with an alkali solution.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.900
Although the tar seems to have kept them alive,

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.170
the subjects appear desiccated,

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.520
as if electrolytes and blood sugars have been drained.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.530
It's over. It's over. You're safe now.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.970
I could be home, enjoying my wife's pasta bazzul.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:42.370
No, you dragged me down here to hunt monsters.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.190
Credit card records don't lie, Animal.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:47.750
Craven and Chapman flew down here and rented a boat in this village.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.290
They found something big. I can smell it.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.300
That tar was eating us?

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.970
Paradoxically, while also keeping...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.640
you alive and the whole time it was draining away the nutrients from your

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:25.940
blood serious good I would not celebrate just yet

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.170
She is, but I hate her already.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:23.980
I'm f***ing on my son!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:11.260
thing saved our lives. Lucky it doesn't hold a grudge. So it survives an airstrike and then it

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:19.470
swims 1,500 miles just to save our sorry butts? Loyalty. Squids this size have never been seen

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:25.190
before, only speculated upon. They must be deep water dwellers. Then what brought them to the

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:29.520
surface? I'm guessing somebody lean, mean, and oh so green.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.340
No, something is not right.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.580
These squids aren't charred like the others.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.380
Something siphoned out all their vital fluids.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:39.920
Meaning Godzilla didn't do this?

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.970
They look like they've been trained.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.630
Just like the fish we found in the tar.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:47.220
Radiation?

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:50.370
These squids may not be the predators we thought they were.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.940
They may be part of a larger food chain,

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.900
processing food for some other natural enemy.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.240
Let me get this straight.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.960
These mutant squid things use this tar gun to break down their...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.870
food, and now something else is sucking them dry?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.160
Any theories, Dr. Teutopolis?

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.970
Audrey, what are you doing here?

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:09.830
My job.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.130
Miss me?

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.680
Can you say abandonment issues?

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:16.170
Ugh.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.190
You must leave. It is too dangerous.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.770
More dangerous than a cab ride through Godzilla's mouth?

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:24.050
Been there, done that.

00:13:24.390 --> 00:13:27.230
There is no telling what sort of predator is feeding off these squid.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.870
What is that?

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.430
Seeing we've found our predator.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.770
See you, compadre.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.210
It just found us!

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:11.620
I think he's weeing off seafood.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.980
It followed the squids to the surface,

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:16.260
and now Godzilla's burned up its food supply.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.160
This patch isn't even a snack.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:28.810
You must stop this thing unless you plan to adopt it.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:29.960
Shut up and...

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:40.070
Just stay here for a while on the nice, cool sand.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:40.750
Come on.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.860
Now it has to find a suitable substitute.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.240
High weights are?

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.250
Let's go, let's go, move!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.540
Get ahead of him.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.500
Next time we rent on your credit card.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:09.950
They make a nice couple.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.320
I'm in team. I'm in team!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.240
bucks on the walking crab cake.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.890
Just the news reports were right. Where'd that thing come from anyway?

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:28.540
Same place as Godzilla. And if you ask me, it's just the tip of the iceberg.

00:17:50.828 --> 00:17:51.528
It's unstable.

00:18:24.732 --> 00:18:25.652
for the price of one.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:29.020
That monster just sacrificed itself for us, Major.

00:18:35.692 --> 00:18:37.432
Bet against the big guy.

00:18:48.172 --> 00:18:49.012
Target acquired.

00:18:49.036 --> 00:18:49.756
and locked on.

00:18:50.156 --> 00:18:50.976
On my signal.

00:18:51.216 --> 00:18:52.196
No, you can't.

00:18:52.296 --> 00:18:53.296
I have my orders.

00:18:53.716 --> 00:18:56.436
Don't you want just one mutation to be on our side?

00:18:56.812 --> 00:18:58.552
Don't make this harder than it needs to be.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:32.500
Whoa.

00:19:38.668 --> 00:19:40.868
Requesting permission to fire on Godzilla.

00:19:41.836 --> 00:19:46.716
He's the only thing that stands between us and every other mutation that comes crawling out of the woodwork.

00:19:47.052 --> 00:19:49.732
And believe me, Major, there will be others.

00:19:52.364 --> 00:19:53.444
Godzilla is dead.

00:19:54.508 --> 00:19:54.768
Sir?

00:19:55.596 --> 00:19:57.696
Repeat, Godzilla is dead.

00:19:58.188 --> 00:19:58.988
Is it clear?

00:19:59.468 --> 00:19:59.988
Yes, sir.

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:02.350
Thank you, Kate.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.500
Don't make me regret this.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:17.700
Destroyed by the U.S. Armed Forces with no loss of life.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.370
This is Audrey Timmons reporting from Jamaica.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:22.550
Thanks for keeping Godzilla out of the spotlight.

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:23.910
It saved our lives.

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.290
I guess I owed it that much.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.390
And all it cost me was an Emmy.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:29.650
Not that I'm bitter.

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.350
I'm just glad it's over.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:33.020
Over?

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:36.040
Just be thankful that whatever we have to face in the future,

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.060
we won't be facing it alone.
